<%# The questions podcasters, brands (and judges) ask, answered plainly. Native <details>, so it works without
    JavaScript. %>
<div class="faq">
  <h2 id="faq-title" class="type-h2">Questions</h2>
  <div class="faq-list">
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">Is listing my show free?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          Yes. Claiming your page, setting your rates, verifying your numbers and answering brands are all free, and
          <%= APP_NAME %> takes no commission on any deal. The paid plans are for the AI sponsor reports and pitch packs.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">How do verified numbers work?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          You invite <%= APP_NAME %>'s stats account to your show: in Spotify for Creators with Analytics access only, or
          in Apple Podcasts Connect with the Analyst role, which can only see analytics. <%= APP_NAME %> then reads your
          numbers with its own account, every day, and labels them "Verified" with the service and the date.
        </p>
        <p>
          You never share a password. Remove the access and the numbers stop updating; after
          <%= StatReading::TTL.in_days.to_i %> days they read "Last verified" instead.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">Where does the data come from?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          A show's page is built from its own RSS feed: episodes, the people it names, and the sponsor reads, promo codes
          and offers in recent show notes, each tied to its episode. Podcast Index helps us find shows. Verified numbers
          come from Spotify for Creators and Apple Podcasts Connect, with the show's permission.
        </p>
        <p>
          Qloo's taste graph tells us what people with a show's taste love more than most people do (brands, music, TV,
          podcasts and places) and how they lean by age and gender. It ranks shows for brands and brands for shows, and
          it's labelled "Taste data from Qloo" wherever it appears. An AI model, reached through OpenRouter, plans the
          research and writes the reasons and pitches from those results.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">Can brands contact me directly?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          No page shows contact details. Brands request a spot through <%= APP_NAME %>, and you hear about it only once
          you've claimed your show. You can decline, block or report any brand. A brand gets
          <%= User::Brands::DAILY_REQUESTS[:unverified] %> requests a day until it verifies a work email at its own domain.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">Is this my real audience?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          A taste profile isn't. It's modeled from Qloo taste data, not measured: it describes people whose tastes match
          your show's, what they love, where they live and how they lean. Age and gender are shown as leans, never as
          percentages. That's strong evidence of fit to show a brand. It isn't a headcount.
        </p>
        <p>
          Verified numbers are different. They come from Spotify or Apple when you invite <%= APP_NAME %>, and they say so.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">What's a proxy profile?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          Many small shows aren't in Qloo's graph yet. When yours isn't, we build the taste profile from comparable shows,
          guests and topics found in your feed, plus any shows you tell us your listeners love. The report labels it a proxy
          profile and lists each of those seeds with where it came from.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">What doesn't a report prove?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          That a brand will say yes, or what it will pay. Fit scores rank brands by shared taste and sponsorship history; they
          aren't a forecast. Downloads are verified only when you invite <%= APP_NAME %>; otherwise they're the numbers you
          enter, labelled as yours. We don't look up contact emails. The pitch pack tells you which role to look for.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">Do you email brands for me?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          No. You send every pitch yourself: copy it, or open it in Gmail. There's no bulk sending, and <%= APP_NAME %> takes
          no commission on any deal you land.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">Who are the sample reports about?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          Public podcasts, researched by the same agent you'd use. Each one is labelled “Sample report. Not affiliated with the
          show.” The shows didn't ask for them and aren't connected to <%= APP_NAME %>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">Can I remove my show's page?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          Yes. Every page has "Remove this page". The show's verified owner removes it at once; anyone else's request is
          reviewed by hand. A removed show isn't added back. The <%= link_to "data sources page", data_sources_path, class: "link" %>
          explains what we keep and why.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">Can I cancel?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          Yes. Monthly and yearly plans cancel from your account page and run to the end of the period you paid for. The
          <%= Entitlements.limits(:sprint)[:name] %> plan is a single payment and never renews.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">What happens to my data?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          Your shows, reports, pitches and notes are visible only to you, unless you publish your listing. Deleting your
          account deletes them. Messages you sent stay in the other side's copy of the conversation, from a deleted
          account. The <%= link_to "privacy page", privacy_path, class: "link" %> has the details.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</div>
